2590               /
2591               /THE FOLLOWING TEST IS A MARCH PATTERN DEVELOPED FOR TESTING
2592               /THE MS8-C MOS MEMORY.
2593               /
2594               /       THE TEST SELECTED FOR THE MOS MEMORY TESTING IS A TYPICAL MARCH
2595               /       PATTERN. THE TEST BEGINS BY LOADING THE ENTIRE MEMORY WITH
2596               /       A 2525 PATTERN. THEN STARTING AT ADDRESS ZERO OF LOWEST POSSIBLE
2597               /       FIELD THE TEST READS THE CONTENTS, COMPARES IT, AND THEN WRITES BACK
2598               /       THE COMPLEMENT VALUE. THE PROCESS IS REPEATED THROUGHOUT THE ENTIRE
2599               /       MEMORY.
2600               /
2601               /       NEXT THE PROCESS REPEATS FROM MAXIMUM TO MINIMUM, COMPLEMENTING
2602               /       AS IT IS BEING DONE.
2603               /
2604               /       THE ENTIRE SEQUENCE IS THEN REPEATED USING A BACKGROUND OF
2605               /       5252. THIS INSURES THAT A ONE AND A ZERO CAN BE WRITTEN INTO
2606               /       EACH MEMORY CELL.
2607               /
2608               /
2609               /
